  "grammar": [
    {
      "title": "Hacer + Weather \u2014 The Go-To Structure",
      "content": "In Spanish, weather expressions use HACER (to make/do):\n\n- Hace sol. (It's sunny.)\n- Hace fr\u00edo. (It's cold.)\n- Hace calor. (It's hot.)\n- Hace viento. (It's windy.)\n- Hace fresco. (It's cool.)\n- Hace buen tiempo. (It's good weather.)\n- Hace mal tiempo. (It's bad weather.)\n\nFor rain/snow, use the verb directly:\n- Llueve. (It's raining.)\n- Nieva. (It's snowing.)\n- Graniza. (It's hailing.)\n\nTo describe current weather:\n- Est\u00e1 lloviendo. (It's raining right now.)\n- Est\u00e1 nublado. (It's cloudy.)\n- Est\u00e1 despejado. (It's clear.)",
      "examples": [
        "Hace calor en verano. (It's hot in summer.)\nHace fr\u00edo en invierno. (It's cold in winter.)\n\u00bfQu\u00e9 tiempo hace hoy? (What's the weather like today?)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Seasons and Weather Expressions",
      "content": "Seasons in Spanish:\n- La primavera (spring)\n- El verano (summer)\n- El oto\u00f1o (autumn/fall)\n- El invierno (winter)\n\nWeather by season:\n- En primavera hace buen tiempo. (In spring it's good weather.)\n- En verano hace mucho calor. (In summer it's very hot.)\n- En oto\u00f1o llueve mucho. (In autumn it rains a lot.)\n- En invierno hace fr\u00edo y puede nevar. (In winter it's cold and it may snow.)\n\n'Puede' = it may/might (from poder)",
      "examples": [
        "En verano voy a la playa. (In summer I go to the beach.)\nEn oto\u00f1o las hojas caen. (In autumn the leaves fall.)"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "pronunciation": [
    {
      "title": "Vowel Length and Consistency",
      "content": "Spanish vowels are always the same length \u2014 no diphthongs unless marked.\n\na = ah, e = eh, i = ee, o = oh, u = oo\n\nThis is different from English where 'a' can be 'ay' (cake) or 'ah' (cat). In Spanish:\n- agua = AH-gwah (always 'ah')\n- cielo = SYEH-loh (always 'eh')\n- libro = LEE-broh (always 'ee')\n- sol = SOH (always 'oh')\n- luna = LOO-nah (always 'oo')",
      "examples": [
        "lluvia (YOO-vee-ah)\nverano (beh-RAH-noh)\nnieve (NYEH-veh)"
      ]
    }
  ],
